    "content": "<!-- wp:cil/page-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Condition · Foreskin emergency \\u0026 circumcision\",\"title\":\"Paraphimosis and Circumcision\",\"lede\":\"Paraphimosis occurs when the foreskin has been pulled back behind the head of the penis (glans) and becomes trapped, so that it cannot be brought forward into its normal position.\",\"reviewedBy\":\"\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/team/#haidar\\u0022\\u003eDr Haidar Al-Ali, BDS, MFDS RCPS (Glasg)\\u003c/a\\u003e, September 2026\",\"crumbs\":[{\"label\":\"Reasons\",\"href\":\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/phimosis/\"},{\"label\":\"Paraphimosis\",\"href\":\"\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section-sm\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section-sm\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:html --><div class=\"callout urgent\"><h2 class=\"display d-3\">Paraphimosis is a medical emergency</h2><p style=\"margin-top:10px\">If your foreskin is currently trapped behind the glans and you cannot return it forwards, do not wait for a routine appointment, callback or message reply from Beverley Clinic. <strong>Seek urgent medical care immediately (NHS 111 / A&amp;E).</strong> As BAUS (British Association of Urological Surgeons) notes, failure to reduce a trapped foreskin promptly can progress from venous congestion and swelling to impaired arterial blood flow and tissue damage.</p><div class=\"btn-row\" style=\"margin-top:16px\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/contact/\">Already had the emergency treated? Contact us about circumcision →</a></div></div><!-- /wp:html --><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The trapped foreskin can act as a tight band around the penis, causing increasing swelling and pain.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Once the paraphimosis has been successfully treated and the swelling has settled, circumcision can be performed to address the tight foreskin and help prevent the same problem happening again.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>At Beverley Clinic in North-West London, we provide circumcision following an episode of paraphimosis for suitable children, teenagers and adults.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/spec-panel {\"eyebrow\":\"Paraphimosis at a glance\",\"rows\":[{\"k\":\"What is paraphimosis?\",\"v\":\"The foreskin is pulled back behind the glans and becomes trapped, so that it cannot return to its normal position.\"},{\"k\":\"What does it look and feel like?\",\"v\":\"The head of the penis and retracted foreskin may become swollen and painful, with a tight band of foreskin sitting behind the glans.\"},{\"k\":\"Is paraphimosis an emergency?\",\"v\":\"Yes. It requires urgent medical treatment.\"},{\"k\":\"Should I book a routine appointment at Beverley Clinic if I have it now?\",\"v\":\"No. Acute paraphimosis requires urgent medical treatment rather than a routine clinic appointment.\"},{\"k\":\"What does Beverley Clinic provide?\",\"v\":\"After the emergency has been treated and the swelling has settled, we can provide circumcision to treat the underlying foreskin problem and help prevent recurrence.\"}],\"note\":\"Circumcision following paraphimosis is assessed individually. See our \\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/prices/\\u0022 style=\\u0022color:var(\\u002d\\u002dblue-deep)\\u0022\\u003eprice list\\u003c/a\\u003e for consultation and surgical fees.\"} /--></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"mechanism-and-symptoms\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"mechanism-and-symptoms\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">What is paraphimosis?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Normally, when a retractable foreskin is pulled backwards over the glans, it should be possible to bring it forwards again so that it returns to its normal position.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>With paraphimosis, the foreskin becomes stuck in the retracted position behind the glans.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The trapped foreskin forms a constricting ring.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>As swelling develops, it can become progressively more difficult to return the foreskin to its normal position.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This is why paraphimosis should not be ignored or left to see whether it improves by itself.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">What are the symptoms of paraphimosis?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Typical features include:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Foreskin trapped behind the glans</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Inability to pull the foreskin forwards again</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Swelling of the glans</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Swelling of the retracted foreskin</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Pain or increasing discomfort</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A tight band of foreskin behind the glans</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Red, dark red, purple or blue discolouration in more severe cases</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>The most important feature is a retracted foreskin that cannot be returned to its normal position over the glans.</strong></p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"emergency-guidance\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\" id=\"emergency-guidance\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">Why is paraphimosis an emergency?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A trapped foreskin can act like a constricting band around the penis.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>As the tissues swell, the constriction can become tighter.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This can interfere with normal blood circulation to the tissues beyond the constricting foreskin.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If severe paraphimosis is left untreated, there is a risk of damage to the tissues from impaired blood supply.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Prompt treatment is therefore essential.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">What should I do if I have paraphimosis now?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If your foreskin is currently trapped behind the glans and you cannot return it to its normal position:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Seek urgent medical treatment.</strong></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Do not wait for a routine appointment at Beverley Clinic and do not delay treatment while waiting for us to respond to an email, WhatsApp message or callback request.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>If you are in the UK, seek urgent NHS medical assistance. If the problem is severe or rapidly worsening, attend an appropriate emergency service (A&amp;E).</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Once the emergency has been treated and swelling has subsided, you can contact us to discuss circumcision.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"causes\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"causes\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Clinical Causes\",\"heading\":\"What causes paraphimosis?\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"Paraphimosis usually occurs when a relatively tight foreskin is pulled backwards over the glans and then cannot be returned forwards.\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Sexual activity\",\"title\":\"Can paraphimosis happen during sex?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eYes. A relatively tight foreskin may retract during sexual activity or masturbation and then become trapped behind the glans.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf you have previously noticed that your foreskin becomes tight, painful or difficult to bring forwards after an erection, this should not be ignored.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf it becomes completely trapped and cannot be returned forwards, seek urgent medical treatment.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/adults/\\u0022\\u003eAdult circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Hygiene \\u0026 cleaning\",\"title\":\"During washing or medical examination\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eParaphimosis frequently occurs when the foreskin is pulled back for washing, personal cleaning, or during a physical examination.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf the foreskin is left retracted rather than immediately returned forward over the glans, swelling can quickly trap it in place.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIt can also happen following catheterisation if the foreskin is not replaced immediately.\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Tight foreskin\",\"title\":\"Underlying phimosis or tightness\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eParaphimosis usually occurs when a relatively tight foreskin is pulled backwards over the glans and then cannot be returned forwards.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThe tight foreskin can pass backwards over the widest part of the glans during retraction, but then struggles to move forwards again once swelling begins.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/phimosis/\\u0022\\u003ePhimosis and tight foreskin →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"32px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\" style=\"margin-top:32px\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Typical situations where paraphimosis can occur include:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>During washing or cleaning</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>During sexual activity</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>During masturbation</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Following examination of the penis</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Following a medical procedure where the foreskin has been retracted</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>In someone who already has a tight foreskin or phimosis</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The swelling that develops can then make the foreskin increasingly difficult to return to its normal position. If you have recurring foreskin tightness without an acute paraphimosis, read:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons {\"className\":\"wp-block-buttons\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"16px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\" style=\"margin-top:16px\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/phimosis/\">Phimosis and tight foreskin →</a></div><!-- /wp:button --><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/adults/\">Adult circumcision →</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"treatment\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"treatment\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">How is acute paraphimosis treated?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The immediate priority is to release the trapped foreskin and restore it to its normal position.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This requires urgent medical assessment.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>In many cases a healthcare professional can reduce the swelling and return the foreskin forwards over the glans.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If this cannot be achieved, an urgent surgical procedure may sometimes be required.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>Beverley Clinic does not provide emergency reduction of acute paraphimosis.</strong></p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our role is different: after the emergency has been successfully treated and the swelling has settled, we can assess the patient for circumcision to prevent the same tight foreskin causing another episode.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">When can circumcision be performed after paraphimosis?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Circumcision is generally planned after the acute paraphimosis has been successfully treated and the significant swelling and inflammation have settled.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The exact timing depends on the individual patient and the condition of the penis and foreskin.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>When you contact us, tell us:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>That you have recently had paraphimosis</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>When the episode occurred</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>How it was treated</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Whether the foreskin is still swollen or inflamed</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Whether you have had paraphimosis before</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Whether you have an underlying tight foreskin</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Whether you have any other foreskin condition</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We can then advise you about assessment and circumcision.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"related-conditions\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"related-conditions\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Clinical Differentiation\",\"heading\":\"Paraphimosis, phimosis and related foreskin conditions\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"Recognising underlying foreskin conditions helps determine the right circumcision technique and prevents recurrence.\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"eyebrow\":\"Differential diagnosis\",\"title\":\"Paraphimosis or phimosis – what is the difference?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eThe names are similar but they describe two different problems.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003ePhimosis\\u003c/strong\\u003e means the foreskin is too tight to retract normally over the glans.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eParaphimosis\\u003c/strong\\u003e means the foreskin has already been retracted but is now trapped behind the glans and cannot be brought forwards again.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003ePhimosis is generally not an emergency unless it prevents urination. Paraphimosis is an emergency because the trapped foreskin can compromise blood flow.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/phimosis/\\u0022\\u003eLearn more about phimosis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Scarred foreskin\",\"title\":\"What if my foreskin is scarred (BXO)?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eIf examination shows that the foreskin is not simply tight but also white, thickened or scarred, there may be an underlying foreskin condition such as BXO / lichen sclerosis.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eThis matters because the abnormal scarred foreskin needs to be recognised when the circumcision is planned so that the affected tissue is appropriately removed.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/bxo/\\u0022\\u003eBXO / lichen sclerosis and circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"eyebrow\":\"Recurrent inflammation\",\"title\":\"What if I also get recurrent balanitis?\",\"html\":\"\\u003cp\\u003eSome patients with a tight foreskin experience repeated episodes of inflammation as well as difficulty retracting the foreskin.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eRecurrent balanitis can lead to scarring and progressive tightness, increasing the risk of subsequent foreskin entrapment.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003eIf recurrent inflammation is part of your history, tell us when booking.\\u003c/p\\u003e\\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/balanitis/\\u0022\\u003eRecurrent balanitis and circumcision →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"}]} /--><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"32px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\" style=\"margin-top:32px\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-3\"} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-3\">What if I have had paraphimosis more than once?</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Repeated episodes are particularly important to mention.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If the foreskin repeatedly becomes trapped behind the glans, the underlying foreskin problem remains present.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Once the current episode has been treated and the tissues have recovered, contact us to discuss circumcision.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Circumcision removes the foreskin permanently and therefore prevents future paraphimosis caused by that foreskin.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"32px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\" style=\"margin-top:32px\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-3\"} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-3\">Is paraphimosis related to a tight foreskin?</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Often, yes.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A relatively tight foreskin can pass backwards over the widest part of the glans but then struggle to move forwards again.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Some patients therefore have a history of phimosis or foreskin tightness before developing paraphimosis.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If there is a tight or scarred foreskin, we take this into account when planning the circumcision.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-warm\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"clinical-assessment\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-warm\" id=\"clinical-assessment\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">Why consider circumcision after paraphimosis?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>An episode of paraphimosis demonstrates that the foreskin has been capable of becoming trapped behind the glans.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If the underlying foreskin remains tight, there is a possibility that the same problem can occur again.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Circumcision permanently removes the foreskin, meaning that the foreskin can no longer become trapped behind the glans in the same way.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>For patients attending Beverley Clinic following paraphimosis, circumcision is the treatment we provide.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">Circumcision following paraphimosis at Beverley Clinic</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Once the acute episode has been treated and the penis has recovered sufficiently, we assess the foreskin before circumcision.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We want to establish whether there is:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"cil-checklist\"} --><ul class=\"cil-checklist wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A persistent tight foreskin</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A defined tight ring</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Foreskin scarring</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>BXO / lichen sclerosis</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Evidence of previous inflammation</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A tight or scarred frenulum</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Another anatomical issue that needs to be considered</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The circumcision is then planned according to the patient's age, anatomy and examination findings.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>For detailed information about the actual circumcision procedure, local anaesthetic, wound closure and recovery, use the appropriate guide rather than repeating it here:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons {\"className\":\"wp-block-buttons\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"16px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\" style=\"margin-top:16px\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/adults/\">Adult circumcision →</a></div><!-- /wp:button --><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/children/\">Circumcision for children and teenagers →</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"recovery-pricing\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"recovery-pricing\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">Recovery after circumcision</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Recovery depends on the patient's age and the circumcision technique used.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>You will receive detailed written aftercare following the procedure and follow-up support during healing.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>For information about swelling, wound care, stitches, activity and when to contact us, see:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons {\"className\":\"wp-block-buttons\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"12px\",\"bottom\":\"20px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\" style=\"margin-top:12px;margin-bottom:20px\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/aftercare/\">Circumcision aftercare →</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>For adults, our clinic generally advises avoiding sexual intercourse and masturbation for at least two weeks and until the wound is sufficiently healed.</strong></p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If healing is incomplete at two weeks, you should wait longer and follow your individual aftercare instructions.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">How much does circumcision after paraphimosis cost?</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Paraphimosis is commonly associated with an underlying medical foreskin problem.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The applicable circumcision price therefore depends on the patient's age and findings on examination.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>For current prices and an explanation of what is included, see:</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons {\"className\":\"wp-block-buttons\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"12px\",\"bottom\":\"20px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\" style=\"margin-top:12px;margin-bottom:20px\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"wp-block-button\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/prices/\">View circumcision prices →</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you are unsure which price applies, contact us and tell us that you have previously been treated for paraphimosis.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"why-choose-us\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section\" id=\"why-choose-us\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/section-head {\"eyebrow\":\"Clinical Expertise\",\"heading\":\"Why choose Beverley Clinic for paraphimosis circumcision?\",\"display\":\"d-2\",\"lede\":\"Dedicated circumcision expertise in North-West London with a patient-centred medical approach.\"} /--><!-- wp:cil/info-cards {\"columns\":\"g-3\",\"headingLevel\":3,\"items\":[{\"title\":\"Specialist circumcision experience\",\"body\":\"Circumcision is a core part of our day-to-day clinical work rather than an occasional procedure. We regularly assess foreskin problems as well as performing circumcisions for medical reasons.\"},{\"title\":\"Recognition of underlying foreskin problems\",\"body\":\"We recognise that paraphimosis often stems from underlying tightness, scarring or BXO. We assess the foreskin carefully before deciding which surgical technique is appropriate.\"},{\"title\":\"Circumcision planned around the problem\",\"body\":\"When circumcision is performed after paraphimosis, we pay particular attention to removing the constricting preputial ring completely to prevent any possibility of recurrence.\"},{\"title\":\"All age groups: children, teenagers and adults\",\"body\":\"We provide circumcision across all age groups, allowing us to understand how foreskin anatomy and surgical techniques differ between paediatric and adult patients.\"},{\"title\":\"Comprehensive aftercare and follow-up\",\"body\":\"Patients receive preparation information before treatment, detailed written aftercare afterwards and clinical follow-up support during the healing process.\"}]} /--></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/faq {\"heading\":\"Frequently asked questions about paraphimosis\",\"items\":[{\"q\":\"Is paraphimosis an emergency?\",\"a\":\"Yes. A foreskin that is trapped behind the glans and cannot be returned forwards requires urgent medical treatment.\"},{\"q\":\"Should I book an appointment with Beverley Clinic if I have paraphimosis right now?\",\"a\":\"No. Do not wait for a routine circumcision appointment. Acute paraphimosis requires urgent medical treatment.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the difference between phimosis and paraphimosis?\",\"a\":\"Phimosis is a foreskin that cannot retract normally. Paraphimosis occurs when the foreskin has been retracted but becomes trapped behind the glans and cannot return forwards. \\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/phimosis/\\u0022\\u003eRead our phimosis guide →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"Why is paraphimosis dangerous?\",\"a\":\"The trapped foreskin can form a constricting band. Increasing swelling can interfere with blood circulation to the penis if the condition is not treated promptly.\"},{\"q\":\"Can paraphimosis go away by itself?\",\"a\":\"You should not wait to see whether acute paraphimosis resolves by itself. If the foreskin is trapped behind the glans and cannot be returned, seek urgent medical treatment.\"},{\"q\":\"Can paraphimosis happen again?\",\"a\":\"Yes. If the underlying tight foreskin remains present, another episode can occur.\"},{\"q\":\"Does circumcision prevent paraphimosis?\",\"a\":\"Circumcision permanently removes the foreskin. Once the foreskin has been completely removed, it cannot subsequently become trapped behind the glans and cause paraphimosis.\"},{\"q\":\"When can I be circumcised after paraphimosis?\",\"a\":\"Circumcision is generally planned after the acute episode has been successfully treated and significant swelling and inflammation have settled. Timing depends on the individual patient and examination.\"},{\"q\":\"What if I have phimosis as well?\",\"a\":\"Phimosis is commonly associated with paraphimosis. We assess the tight foreskin when planning your circumcision. \\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/phimosis/\\u0022\\u003eRead about circumcision for phimosis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"What if my foreskin is white or scarred?\",\"a\":\"A white, thickened or scarred foreskin can suggest BXO / lichen sclerosis and should be recognised before circumcision. \\u003cp\\u003e\\u003ca href=\\u0022https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/conditions/bxo/\\u0022\\u003eRead about BXO / lichen sclerosis →\\u003c/a\\u003e\\u003c/p\\u003e\"},{\"q\":\"What treatment does Beverley Clinic provide after paraphimosis?\",\"a\":\"Once the emergency episode has been treated and the penis has recovered sufficiently, the treatment we provide for the underlying foreskin problem is circumcision.\"}]} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/section {\"size\":\"section\",\"band\":\"bg-card edge\",\"wrap\":\"wrap\",\"anchor\":\"book-consultation\"} --><section class=\"wp-block-cil-section section bg-card edge\" id=\"book-consultation\"><div class=\"wrap\"><!-- wp:cil/split {\"reverse\":false} --><div class=\"wp-block-cil-split split\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"body-text\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group body-text\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2,\"className\":\"wp-block-heading display d-2\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading display d-2\">Circumcision after paraphimosis in London</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you have already received urgent treatment for paraphimosis and would now like to arrange circumcision, contact Beverley Clinic.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Tell us when the paraphimosis occurred, how it was treated and whether you have had previous episodes.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If your foreskin is currently trapped behind the glans, however, do not wait for an appointment with us. Seek urgent medical treatment.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>Beverley Clinic</strong><br>78 Beverley Drive<br>Edgware<br>North-West London<br>HA8 5NE</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons {\"className\":\"wp-block-buttons cil-consultation-buttons-grid\",\"style\":{\"spacing\":{\"margin\":{\"top\":\"24px\"}}}} --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons cil-consultation-buttons-grid\" style=\"margin-top:24px\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/prices/\">View circumcision prices →</a></div><!-- /wp:button --><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/contact/\">Contact Beverley Clinic →</a></div><!-- /wp:button --><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"wp-block-button\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://circumcision-london-wp.vercel.app/book/\">Book an appointment →</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:cil/callback-card {\"eyebrow\":\"Request a call back\",\"title\":\"Ask us first\",\"formId\":\"paraphimosis\",\"subject\":\"Paraphimosis enquiry (post-emergency)\",\"urgent\":false} /--></div><!-- /wp:cil/split --></div></section><!-- /wp:cil/section -->\n\n<!-- wp:cil/cta-b